# openai-compatible_opencode-fix

Re-exports the `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` with full support for PDF, audio, and text file attachments.

## Problem

Related issue: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/16338

OpenCode bundles an outdated version of `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` (OpenCode still use version 1.x.x) that only handles `image/*` file parts. So, when you try to send PDFs, audio, or text files, you will get: `AI_UnsupportedFunctionalityError: 'file part media type application/pdf' functionality not supported.`

This affects custom providers configured in `opencode.json` that use `"npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"`, particularly:
- LiteLLM proxies
- vLLM instances
- Ollama
- Any other OpenAI-compatible API

## Solution

This package re-exports `createOpenAICompatible` from the latest upstream version, which includes full media type support in its chat message converter.

## Usage

1. Install:
```bash
npm install -g openai-compatible_opencode-fix
```

2. Update your ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json:
```
{
  "provider": {
    "litellm": {
      "npm": "openai-compatible_opencode-fix",
      "models": {
        "my-model": {
          "attachment": true,
          "modalities": {
            "input": ["text", "image", "pdf", "audio"],
            "output": ["text"]
          }
          // ...
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

3. Restart OpenCode.

